# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Staff app (app.<domain>) — Vercel project "vms-staff"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite inlines every VITE_ prefixed variable into the client bundle. That is
# correct for these two: the publishable key is meant to be public, and Row
# Level Security is what actually decides access.
VITE_APP_TARGET=staff
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kiosk app (kiosk.<domain>) — Vercel project "vms-kiosk"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tablet holds NO Supabase credentials. These are read only by the functions
# under api/kiosk, which run on the server.
#
# NEVER add a VITE_ prefix to the service role key. Vite would inline it into the
# tablet bundle and hand every visitor full database access.
# VITE_APP_TARGET=kiosk
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
